|term[universal-location]
  :status settled
  :subject-field addressing
  :layer framing-vocabulary
  :gloss A location so fully specified it works as a path from anywhere.
  |designation universal-location
    :status preferred
    :channel prose
  |definition
    :defined-by @def-locations-and-paths
    :anchor universal-location
    :projection paraphrase
    A LOCATION that, due to full specificity, can be used as an effective PATH from anywhere — its components progressively resolve from anywhere to the destination. Equivalently: a PATH with a UNIVERSAL ORIGIN.
  |set-rel :kind subset-of :to @location
  |invariant
    This is the exact condition under which path, location, and identity safely interchange — the "Universal" presupposed by URI/URN/URL, explaining their conflation rather than observing it.
